# Jupyter-deploy: Review CI Infrastructure Template (tf-aws-iam-review)

## Project organization

This project manages AWS resources for automated roborev PR reviews in GitHub
Actions CI. It uses Terraform as the infrastructure-as-code engine and deploys
an ECR repository for the review image and two IAM roles scoped to GitHub
Actions environments.

**IMPORTANT:** The GitHub Actions OIDC provider is a singleton per AWS account.
Only one can exist for `token.actions.githubusercontent.com`. If another deployment
in this account already created it (for example the tf-aws-iam-ci template), set
`create_oidc_provider` to `false` to reference the existing one via data source.

### Resources managed

- **OIDC provider** — GitHub Actions federation (conditional)
- **ECR repository** — stores the roborev review image
- **Publish role** — assumed by the publishing repo's review environment to push the image
- **Run role** — assumed by consumer repos' review environment to pull the image and invoke Bedrock

The run role can only pull the review image and invoke the configured Bedrock
models. This bounds what a prompt-injected review of an untrusted diff can do.

